<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-ANL replaces ship on Australia-SE Asia trade.</title>
<headline>RTRS-ANL replaces ship on Australia-SE Asia trade.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>ANL Ltd, Australia's government-owned line, said it would replace the ANRO Australia with a larger and faster vessel to better service the Australian-Southeast Asian trade.</p>
<p>The new vessel would be named Australian Enterprise.</p>
<p>The purchased container vessel was built in 1985, has a capability of lifting about 34,000 tonnes deadweight and can accommodate up to 350 containers at a service speed of more than 21 knots, ANL said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
